WEBVTT

00:01:59.246 --> 00:02:03.579
to access the ever-expanding big data
stored at CERN without traveling,

00:02:03.621 --> 00:02:06.246
the networks needed 
to be talking in the same language.

00:02:06.288 --> 00:02:09.871
We adopted the fledgling internet
working standard from the States,

00:02:09.913 --> 00:02:11.829
followed by the rest of Europe

00:02:11.871 --> 00:02:13.996
and we established
the principal link at CERN

00:02:14.038 --> 00:02:16.954
between Europe and the States in 1989,

00:02:16.996 --> 00:02:19.954
and the truly global internet took off!

00:02:20.204 --> 00:02:24.371
Physicists could easily then access
the terabytes of Big Data

00:02:24.413 --> 00:02:27.204
remotely from around the world,
generate results,

00:02:27.246 --> 00:02:30.746
and write papers in their home institutes.